
  Read wtm's daemon, the one process of this machine that runs the jobs of every
  repository, serves their named addresses and carries the event stream: whether
  it runs and its pid, its build against this wtm's, the jobs it holds by repository
  and worktree, the port of its proxy, its socket and its index of jobs.

  With none running, the stacks and the holds on shared services its index keeps,
  which run on without it. It changes nothing and never starts the daemon.

  Usage:
    wtm-next status [flags]

  Examples:
    wtm daemon status

    wtm daemon status --output json

  Flags:
    -h, --help            help for status
        --output string   Output format: text or json (default "text")

  Global Flags:
    -q, --quiet   Silence human output; errors and the exit code are unaffected, and --output json still emits its document

